{"id": "EUVD-2026-52327", "enisaUuid": "d0e52b38-de50-3e30-8d09-14c008c8897e", "description": "A flaw was found in GNU tar. When extracting an archive with the --one-top-level option, hardlink targets are not confined to the designated top-level directory and may resolve relative to the extraction working directory. A crafted archive can create hardlinks that escape the intended boundary and, when combined with a preexisting symbolic link under the working directory, may allow writing outside that boundary during a single extraction.", "datePublished": "2026-08-03T14:51:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-22T21:29:46", "baseScore": 4.4, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:50807", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:61581", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:61586", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:61783", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:66018", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:70390", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-18508", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2509843"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-18508", "GHSA-4f5j-wqjr-hx49"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05fe50e8-2050-30c1-9213-41ee82f5c77b", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Update Infrastructure 5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1788765051"}, {"id": "172997f6-a208-3b5d-8ba1-3d5e4d84bfa1", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Update Infrastructure 5", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1788880456"}, {"id": "199ccf7a-54f6-3fd4-8a0f-24b5728bdacd", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 2:1.30-13.el8_10"}, {"id": "20c0f05f-3fca-372f-b9b8-6ce55d441bc7", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 2:1.35-13.el10_2"}, {"id": "349d63ea